{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Group - Privilege - Administrator Privileges Assigned to an Okta Group",
	"Description": "An administrator role was granted to an Okta group. Granting at the group level is quieter than granting to a user, because the adversary can then add themselves to the group and inherit the role without another privilege event.\n\nEvent type: group.privilege.grant\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/persistence_administrator_privileges_assigned_to_okta_group/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/persistence_administrator_privileges_assigned_to_okta_group.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "8a82332e-d777-5f3c-9433-d6deb454abf2",
	"SearchReference": "ee336fb2-281f-5187-ad7f-c0e709761cfc"
